source: ASF Jira Server 8.20.10, POST /rest/api/1.0/render (hack/jira-render-evidence.py), captured 2026-08-22
observed: Jira reads the inner hyphens as a strikethrough pair rather than dashes, so jiro warns about the effect.
-- input.jira --
{{a--b--c}}
-- rendered.html --
<p><tt>a-<del>b</del>-c</tt></p>
-- want.md --
`a--b--c`
-- warnings.json --
[
 {
  "Line": 1,
  "Column": 1,
  "Construct": "inline-code",
  "Reason": "Jira would render a strikethrough effect inside this Monospace Span; inline code keeps the characters literal"
 }
]
